<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Aram-Damascus</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 BCE – 732 BCE (approx.) · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Aram-Damascus, the strongest Aramaean kingdom, which led Syria against Assyria and dominated Israel under King Hazael.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>, Aramaean groups took over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> oasis, once Egyptian Upi. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Bible</a> credits <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rezon">Rezon</a>, a fugitive officer of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aram-zobah">Aram-Zobah</a>, with founding the kingdom in the 10th century BCE, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ben-hadad-i">Ben-Hadad I</a> it became the leading power of southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> over the oasis and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hauran">Hauran</a>, controlling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadadezer-of-damascus">Hadadezer</a> led the coalition with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hamath">Hamath</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shalmaneser-iii">Shalmaneser III</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-qarqar">Qarqar</a> in 853 BCE. The usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazael">Hazael</a> then conquered much of Israel and destroyed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gath">Gath</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tel-dan-stele">Tel Dan stele</a> probably records his victories.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rezin">Rezin</a> allied with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a> against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-judah">Judah</a>, whose king appealed to Tiglath-Pileser III of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 732 BCE, killed Rezin and made Aram an Assyrian province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1000 BCE – 732 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:39.80%;width:5.33%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 BCE – 732 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hadadezer, Hazael, Rezin</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Aramaean religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Aram, Aram</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-866&amp;focus=aram-damascus" aria-label="Aram-Damascus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Aram-Damascus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5898 1280M5927 1218L6092 1134M5927 1218L5913 1238"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5898 1280h